stateDiagram-v2
    state "Step 1: Intake — task registered [INTAKE]" as INTAKE
    state "Step 2: Interview — understanding what you want [INTERVIEW]" as INTERVIEW
    state "Step 3: Draft plan authored [DRAFT_PLAN]" as DRAFT_PLAN
    state "Step 4: Plan disposition & acceptance gate [PLAN_REVIEW]" as PLAN_REVIEW
    state "Step 5: Independent plan review — 0 or more rounds [MULTI_AGENT_REVIEW]" as MULTI_AGENT_REVIEW
    state "Step 6: Awaiting your approval [AWAITING_APPROVAL]" as AWAITING_APPROVAL
    state "Step 7: Approved — you said go [APPROVED]" as APPROVED
    state "Step 8: Implementation (isolated worktree) [IN_WORKTREE]" as IN_WORKTREE
    state "Step 9: Here's what changed — initial review [WORKTREE_REVIEW]" as WORKTREE_REVIEW
    state "Step 10: Multi-agent code review — 1 or N rounds [MULTI_AGENT_CODE_REVIEW]" as MULTI_AGENT_CODE_REVIEW
    state "Step 11: Verifying (tests, checks) [VERIFY_EXIT]" as VERIFY_EXIT
    state "Step 12: Retrospective — survey questions [RETROSPECTIVE]" as RETROSPECTIVE
    state "Step 13: Done [DONE]" as DONE
    state "Rolled back — problem found, documented [ROLLED_BACK]" as ROLLED_BACK
    state "Escalated to you for a decision [ESCALATED]" as ESCALATED

    [*] --> INTAKE
    INTAKE --> INTERVIEW
    INTAKE --> DRAFT_PLAN : skip straight to planning
    INTAKE --> PLAN_REVIEW : skip straight to planning
    INTAKE --> ESCALATED
    INTAKE --> DONE : CLOSURE GATE — human-signed transition_request

    INTERVIEW --> DRAFT_PLAN : interview complete<br/>no plan artifacts required yet
    INTERVIEW --> PLAN_REVIEW : legacy/direct plan submission path<br/>(artifacts required)
    INTERVIEW --> RETROSPECTIVE : trivial path — interview baseline<br/>and adaptive follow-ups complete
    INTERVIEW --> ESCALATED
    INTERVIEW --> INTAKE : human-approved recovery reset
    INTERVIEW --> DONE : CLOSURE GATE — human-signed transition_request

    DRAFT_PLAN --> PLAN_REVIEW : submit plan<br/>ask additional review? yes/no
    PLAN_REVIEW --> DRAFT_PLAN : changes requested<br/>revise artifact identity
    DRAFT_PLAN --> INTERVIEW : needs more questions
    PLAN_REVIEW --> INTERVIEW : needs more questions

    PLAN_REVIEW --> MULTI_AGENT_REVIEW : yes — ask method, then internal runtime/model/effort<br/>one at a time, repeat if needed
    PLAN_REVIEW --> AWAITING_APPROVAL : no / plan accepted<br/>continue to human approval
    DRAFT_PLAN --> ESCALATED
    DRAFT_PLAN --> INTAKE : human-approved recovery reset
    DRAFT_PLAN --> DONE : CLOSURE GATE — human-signed transition_request
    PLAN_REVIEW --> ESCALATED
    PLAN_REVIEW --> INTAKE : human-approved recovery reset
    PLAN_REVIEW --> DONE : CLOSURE GATE — human-signed transition_request

    MULTI_AGENT_REVIEW --> PLAN_REVIEW : review complete<br/>merge outcomes for plan acceptance
    MULTI_AGENT_REVIEW --> DRAFT_PLAN : reviewer requested changes<br/>new identity required before resubmission
    MULTI_AGENT_REVIEW --> ESCALATED
    MULTI_AGENT_REVIEW --> INTAKE : human-approved recovery reset
    MULTI_AGENT_REVIEW --> DONE : CLOSURE GATE — human-signed transition_request

    %% CRITICAL HUMAN GATE 1 (cryptographic)
    AWAITING_APPROVAL --> APPROVED : CRITICAL HUMAN GATE 1 (signed) -<br/>human signs the transition_request<br/>(ssh-keygen -Y sign, passphrase prompt)<br/>Releases worktree & coding authority
    AWAITING_APPROVAL --> DRAFT_PLAN : needs more work
    AWAITING_APPROVAL --> PLAN_REVIEW : needs more work
    AWAITING_APPROVAL --> ESCALATED
    AWAITING_APPROVAL --> INTAKE : human-approved recovery reset
    AWAITING_APPROVAL --> DONE : CLOSURE GATE — human-signed transition_request

    APPROVED --> IN_WORKTREE
    APPROVED --> RETROSPECTIVE : human-approved skip implementation
    APPROVED --> ESCALATED
    APPROVED --> INTAKE : human-approved recovery reset
    APPROVED --> DONE : CLOSURE GATE — human-signed transition_request

    IN_WORKTREE --> WORKTREE_REVIEW : implementation + tests done
    IN_WORKTREE --> ROLLED_BACK
    IN_WORKTREE --> ESCALATED
    IN_WORKTREE --> INTAKE : human-approved recovery reset
    IN_WORKTREE --> DONE : CLOSURE GATE — human-signed transition_request

    WORKTREE_REVIEW --> MULTI_AGENT_CODE_REVIEW : yes — choose method<br/>then internal runtime/model/effort one at a time
    
    %% CRITICAL HUMAN GATE 3b (cryptographic)
    WORKTREE_REVIEW --> VERIFY_EXIT : CRITICAL HUMAN GATE 3b (signed) -<br/>human signs acceptance bound to commit SHA,<br/>diff hash and untracked-files hash
    WORKTREE_REVIEW --> IN_WORKTREE : more changes needed
    WORKTREE_REVIEW --> ROLLED_BACK
    WORKTREE_REVIEW --> ESCALATED
    WORKTREE_REVIEW --> INTAKE : human-approved recovery reset
    WORKTREE_REVIEW --> DONE : CLOSURE GATE — human-signed transition_request

    MULTI_AGENT_CODE_REVIEW --> WORKTREE_REVIEW : review package ready<br/>for artifact/scope confirmation
    
    %% CRITICAL HUMAN GATE 3c (cryptographic)
    MULTI_AGENT_CODE_REVIEW --> VERIFY_EXIT : CRITICAL HUMAN GATE 3c (signed) -<br/>human signs acceptance of the reviewed code<br/>(same bound request as 3b)
    MULTI_AGENT_CODE_REVIEW --> IN_WORKTREE : synthesis says bounded changes<br/>human approves rework
    MULTI_AGENT_CODE_REVIEW --> ROLLED_BACK
    MULTI_AGENT_CODE_REVIEW --> ESCALATED
    MULTI_AGENT_CODE_REVIEW --> INTAKE : human-approved recovery reset
    MULTI_AGENT_CODE_REVIEW --> DONE : CLOSURE GATE — human-signed transition_request

    VERIFY_EXIT --> RETROSPECTIVE : ledger + full/task tests + leak check<br/>and map-debt evidence pass
    VERIFY_EXIT --> IN_WORKTREE : verification failed
    VERIFY_EXIT --> WORKTREE_REVIEW : verification failed
    VERIFY_EXIT --> ROLLED_BACK
    VERIFY_EXIT --> ESCALATED
    VERIFY_EXIT --> INTAKE : human-approved recovery reset
    VERIFY_EXIT --> DONE : CLOSURE GATE — human-signed transition_request

    RETROSPECTIVE --> DONE : CLOSURE GATE — human-signed transition_request<br/>binds the retrospective digest<br/>follow-ups resolved
    RETROSPECTIVE --> ESCALATED : retrospective blocked
    RETROSPECTIVE --> INTAKE : human-approved recovery reset
    ROLLED_BACK --> ESCALATED
    ROLLED_BACK --> PLAN_REVIEW : restart planning
    ROLLED_BACK --> INTAKE : human-approved recovery reset
    ROLLED_BACK --> DONE : CLOSURE GATE — human-signed transition_request
    ROLLED_BACK --> RETROSPECTIVE : human-approved recovery reset

    ESCALATED --> INTAKE : start over
    ESCALATED --> PLAN_REVIEW : restart planning
    ESCALATED --> DONE : CLOSURE GATE — human-signed transition_request
    ESCALATED --> RETROSPECTIVE : human-approved recovery reset

    DONE --> INTAKE : human-approved recovery reset
    DONE --> RETROSPECTIVE : human-approved recovery reset
    INTAKE --> RETROSPECTIVE : human-approved recovery reset
    DRAFT_PLAN --> RETROSPECTIVE : human-approved recovery reset
    MULTI_AGENT_REVIEW --> RETROSPECTIVE : human-approved recovery reset
    PLAN_REVIEW --> RETROSPECTIVE : human-approved recovery reset
    AWAITING_APPROVAL --> RETROSPECTIVE : human-approved recovery reset
    IN_WORKTREE --> RETROSPECTIVE : human-approved recovery reset
    WORKTREE_REVIEW --> RETROSPECTIVE : human-approved recovery reset
    MULTI_AGENT_CODE_REVIEW --> RETROSPECTIVE : human-approved recovery reset
    DONE --> [*]

    note right of APPROVED
        Critical Gate 1 (cryptographic):
        Unlocks file write authority and isolated
        worktree execution. Only a verified OpenSSH
        signature (ssh-keygen -Y sign) over the
        transition_request advances this edge.
    end note

    note right of WORKTREE_REVIEW
        Critical Gate 3b & 3c (cryptographic):
        Entering VERIFY_EXIT requires a human signature over
        commit SHA + tracked-diff hash + untracked-files hash.
        The request is verified and consumed once, inside the
        commit transaction. No skip flag, receipt, typed word
        or actor string can substitute; there is no SQLite
        trigger that trusts an actor column for this gate.
    end note

    note right of DONE
        Every edge into DONE -- normal closure and early
        close from any active state -- requires the same
        human-signed transition_request. There is no
        force-close string, flag or confirmation question.
    end note

    note right of IN_WORKTREE
        After APPROVED → IN_WORKTREE, the
        implementation controller runs dispatch,
        review, synthesis, and bounded fixes without
        asking for routine lifecycle transitions.
        Re-enter review only after focused tests and
        the session-wide change inventory pass.

        No direct IN_WORKTREE -> VERIFY_EXIT edge exists.
        A "Gate 3d" fix once gated that edge with a human
        question instead of removing it; the edge was removed
        entirely (2026-09-17): all work passes through
        WORKTREE_REVIEW first.
    end note

    note right of MULTI_AGENT_CODE_REVIEW
        Plan-review receipts and implementation-review
        receipts are isolated. Every reviewer report is
        preserved, synthesized into one revision brief,
        and a requested change returns through the
        human-approved IN_WORKTREE rework edge.
    end note